    's10' => [
        'opening' => [
            'This guide brings together a few familiar observations and manageable options for an ordinary difficult day. It is an everyday wellbeing reference, not an emergency response or a clinical safety plan. If the situation needs urgent or specialist help, access that help without completing these steps.',
        ],
        'step1_heading' => 'Step 1: Notice what is happening',
        'step1' => [
            'TH' => 'When things are especially difficult, you may notice hurt or a stronger need for care. Acknowledge what you are feeling alongside what is happening around you. A difficult feeling deserves attention without becoming a verdict about you.',
            'TF' => 'When things are especially difficult, you may notice intense feelings or an urge to act. Where the situation allows, pause long enough to consider the immediate need and the likely effect of your next response.',
            'BS' => 'When things are especially difficult, you may notice a wish for space or fewer demands. Notice the room around you and what you need now. Quiet can be useful; it does not decide every practical or support need.',
            'BP' => 'When things are especially difficult, you may notice more effort or tighter standards. Where the situation allows, pause to check the task, your capacity and one thing that can wait or be made more manageable.',
            'A' => 'When things are especially difficult, you may recognise a capacity to pause and consider what you need. Use that capacity alongside the actual demands and resources available, without expecting yourself to manage everything.',
            'neutral' => 'Notice what is happening, what you need and what the situation is asking of you. Choose one manageable consideration, recognising when a self-guided activity is not enough.',
        ],
        'pressure' => 'You selected putting pressure on yourself to get everything right, even when things are difficult. Notice whether extra checking or effort is serving the task’s purpose and whether a realistic stopping point would help. This line is not shown merely because Pushing Through is the primary result.',
        'step2_heading' => 'Step 2: Try one familiar small thing',
        'step2' => [
            '6.5.a' => 'You selected time alone as helpful. Take a brief pause from a manageable demand where your circumstances allow it. Notice what some space offers and what still needs attention.',
            '6.5.b' => 'You selected a trusted person as helpful. When that contact is available and safe, choose a brief form of connection that fits what you need and what you want to share.',
            '6.5.c' => 'You selected movement as helpful. If your ability and circumstances allow, try a brief, comfortable movement, such as a gentle stretch, a short walk or a change of position. Keep it manageable for you.',
            '6.5.d' => 'You selected getting outdoors as helpful. If the setting and circumstances are suitable, spend a brief moment outside and notice what is around you. Choose an accessible, manageable option.',
            '6.5.e' => 'You selected listening to music as helpful. Choose a familiar song or piece that fits the moment and give it your attention for a brief time. Notice what the experience offers.',
            '6.5.f' => 'You selected writing as helpful. Privately note one thought, feeling or practical concern that matters now, where doing so is suitable for your device and surroundings. Use the information you want to keep; private details are not required.',
            '6.5.g' => 'You selected quiet as helpful. Take a brief pause in a suitable setting and notice what you need. Keep the experience comfortable rather than trying to force a particular feeling.',
            '6.5.h' => 'You selected something creative as helpful. Spend a brief time on a manageable part of a familiar creative activity, such as drawing, music or making something. Keep the scale realistic for the moment.',
            '6.5.i' => 'You selected time with an animal as helpful. If a familiar animal is nearby and the interaction is suitable for both of you, spend a brief time sitting with them or enjoying their company.',
            '6.5.j' => 'You selected something practical as helpful. Choose one small, comfortable task, such as preparing a drink, washing one item or getting something ready for later. Give the action a clear stopping point.',
            '6.5.k' => 'You selected humour as helpful. Choose a familiar lighthearted moment, such as a short video or a memory that you enjoy. Let the experience be what it is rather than making a changed mood the measure of success.',
            '6.5.l' => 'You selected rest as helpful. Where your circumstances allow, take a brief break in a comfortable position and notice what you need. Rest can be useful alongside responsibilities that remain.',
            '6.5.m' => 'You selected family as helpful. When a particular connection is available and safe, choose a brief form of company that fits the moment and your preferences about what to share.',
        ],
        'step2_none' => 'Your saved answers do not identify one named activity for this step. Choose a brief, manageable option from the existing activity choices, or leave the step for another time. This is a general option, not a claim about what you previously reported as helpful.',
