    'restricted' => [
        's4_help_TH' => 'It can help to treat these moments as a signal to notice what you need, rather than a verdict about you. Feelings matter, but they do not tell the whole story about you or your circumstances. Comfort might come from a familiar independent activity or some quiet. Notice which forms of care are useful, and consider an appropriate professional support route when needed.',
        's4_help_TF' => 'A brief pause can create room to consider what to do next. Notice the energy, the situation and the effect of your response. Privately consider a proportionate adjustment within your influence; this activity does not ask you to contact anyone or repair an unavailable relationship.',
        's4_help_BP' => 'A deliberate pause can help you check what needs your attention and what can wait, be reduced or be done to a good-enough standard. Choose a pause that fits the situation while recognising obligations and limits that cannot be changed alone.',
        's4_happens_A' => 'You might pause, review your options, make a workable plan or adjust what you are asking of yourself. Rest, practical changes or appropriate professional support may be useful, depending on your circumstances. Personal contact is not assumed to be available.',
        'pair_TF_A_repair' => 'If you decide an adjustment is needed, privately identify the impact and what is within your influence. Contact with another person is not part of this activity.',
        's6_4.1.b' => 'Going quiet can give you space to rest, gather your thoughts or reduce demands for a while. Notice how you feel afterwards and whether the space helps you respond to what you need. If another need remains, consider a manageable independent activity, a practical adjustment or an appropriate professional support route.',
        's6_4.1.e' => 'You selected reaching out as a response you recognise. Your current answers also say personal support is unavailable. The report keeps both answers without assuming there is someone you can contact now. Consider a manageable independent response or an appropriate professional support route where needed.',
        's6_4.1.h' => 'You recognise that responses to other people can become short or sharp when things are difficult. Notice the circumstances and the effect of your words or actions. Where the situation allows, pause and privately consider what you would like to do differently. This reflection keeps responsibility in view without requiring direct contact or reconciliation.',
        's6_4.1.k' => 'Comfort or reassurance can matter when things are difficult or uncertain, even when personal support is unavailable. Notice what you need and whether a familiar independent activity, quiet or practical information helps. If the need goes beyond that activity, consider an appropriate professional support route. An unavailable person remains unavailable regardless of how clearly you identify the need.',
        's10_step3' => 'Some situations need more help than an everyday activity can provide. Identify an appropriate professional support route or the information needed to find one. Record unavailable options honestly. Professional, specialist and urgent support access is separate from completing this guide.',
    ],
